WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:02.633
Fit is defined, tested and signed.

00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:05.067
Now define a won deal
and a quarter's revenue.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:07.733
When two screens show two
numbers for one quarter,

00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:12.100
trust in the dashboard dies. Here,
finance and RevOps read one number.

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:15.600
Over the next few minutes you'll
map your CRM's stages onto journeys,

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.000
point revenue at one source,
and choose how credit is shared.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.167
You'll also set currency
rules and your own deal words.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.967
Leo's CRM has a stage
called Closed Renewed.

00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:26.700
A tool that guesses files it as open,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.133
and Mia's pipeline swells with deals
already won. Orbit counts them again.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:34.733
One revenue truth, your words
for stages, and nothing guessed.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.767
First, journeys. In the
console: Settings, Journeys.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:42.367
Define the lifecycles your companies,
people and deals follow: main,

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.300
renewal, self serve, partner.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.733
Each journey has stages
marked open, won or lost,

00:00:46.733 --> 00:00:50.633
and can link to the stages of a deal
pipeline from Settings, Pipelines.

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:54.767
Saving proposes a new version in dev
for a different person to approve.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:58.033
It goes live once signed
and promoted to production.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.467
Your CRM has its own stage values. A
stage map says what each one means.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:05.600
Map it to a journey stage,
ignore it, or press Guess for me.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.900
That suggests from names,
synonyms and won or lost wording,

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.800
ranked by your model if you have one.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.933
Values nobody has decided
are held, never defaulted.

00:01:14.933 --> 00:01:16.667
Those records stay where they are,

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:19.233
and each value raises a
decision for a person.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.033
Or ask your agent: "Which CRM
stage values have no meaning yet,

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:24.300
and where would you put each".

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.967
It lists them with record
counts and a suggestion.

00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:29.900
What a value means is your
call, not the agent's,

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.533
and records follow only
after the map is applied.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.133
Second, revenue truth.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:38.067
In the console: Settings, Money,
Where does revenue truth live.

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:42.067
Pick one source: CRM deal amounts,
warehouse orders or billing records.

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:44.000
The revenue K P I, the dashboard,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.367
attribution and your agents
all read revenue from it.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:50.800
So two screens can't quietly
disagree about one quarter.

00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:53.167
Reconciliation then
compares that truth with

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.900
the won deal amounts in your CRM,

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.567
by month and by account. It lists
the accounts that drift most.

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:59.867
Drift isn't hidden or averaged away.

00:01:59.867 --> 00:02:02.800
It's a list for finance and
RevOps to work through together.

00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:06.533
Third, attribution. In the console:
Settings, Money, Attribution.

00:02:06.533 --> 00:02:10.133
The window is how far back a
touch can claim credit: seven,

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:12.167
thirty or ninety days, or your own number.

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:15.200
The model is how credit
splits across touches.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:19.200
Equal split is the default until
you choose, with position based,

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.167
first touch, last touch
and time decay beside it.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.533
Compare models shows the
same revenue under each.

00:02:24.533 --> 00:02:28.167
Changing either recomputes reports
and rewrites nothing stored.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.867
Two details matter for trust.

00:02:29.867 --> 00:02:32.333
Visits from AI assistants
are classified as

00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:34.567
AI answers and credited to SEO and GEO.

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:37.800
Ad click ids are opt in,
expire after ninety days,

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.467
and are blocked when Global
Privacy Control is on.

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:42.267
They're never shown to agents.

00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:43.533
Or ask your agent:

00:02:43.533 --> 00:02:45.567
"Credit last quarter's revenue to channels

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.433
under equal split and under last touch,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.733
and tell me what changes".

00:02:48.733 --> 00:02:51.467
It shows which channels move
and which window it used.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:54.933
Pro move: run that comparison
before you change the default model.

00:02:54.933 --> 00:02:57.000
Switching it is a person's decision.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:03:00.767
Fourth, currency. In the console:
Settings, Money, Currency and FX rates.

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:04.000
Pick the reporting currency
and the convention:

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.833
your finance team's dated
rates, or daily market rates.

00:03:06.833 --> 00:03:09.667
Add the finance rate sheet month by month,

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.667
and the page shows revenue at
both, with the drift between them.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:15.400
Stored deal values are never rewritten.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.900
The convention applies
when a report is read.

00:03:17.967 --> 00:03:19.767
Last, your words for deals.

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:23.267
In the console: Settings,
Money, Your words for deals.

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:25.767
The OS adopts your words,
and you never adopt ours.

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:29.033
Name your deal types, say new
business, expansion and renewal,

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:34.467
and list the CRM values for each.
Synced deals are typed automatically,

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:37.600
and every dashboard filter
and grouping uses your labels.

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:41.500
Or ask your agent: "What was revenue
last quarter at finance rates,

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.833
and how far is it from
the CRM's won deals".

00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:46.933
It reads in your reporting
currency, shows the drift,

00:03:46.933 --> 00:03:48.767
and reconciles against the CRM.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:51.433
Changing these settings
is for owners and admins.

00:03:51.433 --> 00:03:54.200
The agent reads, explains and proposes.

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:58.133
Fair concern: another settings page
won't end the argument with finance.

00:03:58.133 --> 00:03:59.633
It makes the argument small.

00:03:59.633 --> 00:04:03.033
Reconciliation names the accounts
that drift, month by month.

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:06.667
Nothing stored is rewritten, so you
can change a convention and compare.

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:10.600
And a value nobody has defined is
held for a decision, never guessed.

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:13.800
Replay: Map stages, and
hold what's undecided.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.900
Pick one revenue source and reconcile it.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.233
Compare attribution
models before you switch.

00:04:18.233 --> 00:04:22.033
One revenue truth, your words
for stages, and nothing guessed.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:25.633
You now have stages that mean what
you say, revenue that reconciles,

00:04:25.633 --> 00:04:28.433
and attribution you can inspect.

00:04:28.433 --> 00:04:31.600
Open Settings, then Money, and
pick your revenue source today.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.500
Next: voice, proof and claims.
